+---
+title: 'Stepper progress reflects restored-draft completeness (resume green-lies)'
+type: 'bugfix'
+created: '2026-08-04'
+status: 'done'
+baseline_commit: '42f600d4b84fde29651f3e9eb00d8a695eae84da'
+review_loop_iteration: 0
+context: []
+---
+
+<frozen-after-approval reason="human-owned intent — do not modify unless human renegotiates">
+
+## Intent
+
+**Problem:** After a save-resume restore, the stepper's green progress segments lie in both directions: restored-and-complete steps render white (nothing is seeded on arrival), and any step visited-then-left renders green regardless of content (an empty step 3 turns green the moment you Back out of it). Root cause: the done-set is `visited` — a visit log — not a completeness check. User-reported on the upgraded form; reproduced by Gru with screenshots.
+
+**Approach:** Derive the green state from actual field content, reusing the stepper's own gating rule (`findInvalidControls`): seed the done-set from restored values on the `form-resume` render, and re-derive a step's done state from its live content every time it is left — never from the visit itself.
+
+## Boundaries & Constraints
+
+**Always:**
+- Reuse `findInvalidControls` as the completeness rule — do not duplicate the visible-required logic (briefing: "reuse, don't duplicate").
+- A step left with any unfilled visible-required control must render white — empty-visit-and-leave can NEVER turn a segment green.
+- A step complete at restore must render green ON ARRIVAL (before any navigation).
+- `form-errors` seeds nothing (banner owns attention — existing F1 decision). Pristine `form` also seeds nothing: guarantor-without-`has_guarantor` and tell_us_more are vacuously complete (zero visible-required controls) and would glow green on a fresh form — a new lie. Seeding is resume-only; leave-recompute applies on all three renders.
+- The consent checkbox is `aria-required` only (submit-gated by form.js), invisible to `findInvalidControls` — completeness for the section containing `#gdpr-consent` additionally requires consent checked.
+- Active step keeps precedence (renders amber, not green).
+- Progressive enhancement only; no changes to the POST path, server validation, or the F3 save/restore contract. Fix is confined to `form_stepper.js` + node tests, pure internals exported for `node --test` per the file's existing pattern.
+
+**Ask First:**
+- Expanding green semantics beyond "gating-complete" (e.g. requiring engagement for vacuous-complete sections) — deferred unless the user wants it; called out in the PR.
+
+**Never:**
+- Never change `apply_analytics.js` (W0 funnel contract — visit/interaction-based by design, already suppressed on resume).
+- Never persist done-state or touch the draft payload/server endpoints; never weaken the `?stepper=off` hook or the formJsRan gate.
+
+## I/O & Edge-Case Matrix
+
+| Scenario | Input / State | Expected Output / Behavior | Error Handling |
+|----------|--------------|---------------------------|----------------|
+| Resume, steps 1–2 fully restored | marker `form-resume`, steps 1–2 complete, start at 3 | Segments 1–2 green on arrival; 3 active; 4,7,8 white | N/A |
+| Resume, partial restore (step 2 missing one required field) | marker `form-resume` | Step 2 white on arrival; start lands on step 2 (firstIncompleteIndex already does this) | N/A |
+| Leave an EMPTY step via Back | current step has unfilled visible-required controls | Left step stays white | N/A |
+| Leave a FILLED step via Back/Continue/anchor | all visible-required filled | Left step turns green | N/A |
+| Un-fill a field on a green step, then leave | was complete → now incomplete | Step returns to white (done state is re-derived, never sticky) | N/A |
+| Resume with consent unchecked | review_consent section has no `[required]` controls | Review segment NOT green (consent guard) | N/A |
+| Vacuous-complete sections on resume (guarantor w/o guarantor, tell_us_more) | zero visible-required controls | Green on arrival (gating-mirror; called out in PR) | N/A |
+| form-errors re-render | marker `form-errors`, mid-form start | No segments seeded green; greens accrue only by leaving complete steps | N/A |
+| Pristine form first paint | marker `form`, all empty | All segments white (no seeding) | N/A |
+
+</frozen-after-approval>
+
+## Code Map
+
+- `server/priv/static/form_stepper.js` — the fix surface: `visited` map in `initBrowser` (lines ~"Steps actually visited" block), `show()`, `updateProgress()`; new pure exports `sectionComplete` + `seedDoneStates`.
+- `scripts/js-tests/form_stepper.test.js` — node tests for the new pure functions; fake-DOM `matches()` needs `#id` selector support added (for the `#gdpr-consent` lookup).
+- `server/src/application/form_pages.gleam` — resume render context only (`data-apply-page="form-resume"`; no change).
+- `server/priv/static/form.css` — segment classes (`.stepper-segment` / `-done` / `-active`); no change.
+- `.pi/skills/form-bug-hunt/scenarios/save-resume/round-trip.yaml` — canonical E2E resume drive (token seam via local DB); the browser replay follows its shape.
+
+## Tasks & Acceptance
+
+**Execution:**
+- [x] `server/priv/static/form_stepper.js` — add exported pure predicates `sectionComplete(sectionEl)` (gating rule + `#gdpr-consent` guard), `seedDoneStates(sectionEls, marker)` (resume-only seeding; `{}` for `form`/`form-errors`) and `rederiveDone(done, index, sectionEl)` (leave rule); in `initBrowser` replace the `visited` map with a `done` map seeded via `seedDoneStates`, and in `show()` re-derive the leaving step via `rederiveDone` whenever the index actually changes — root fix for both lie directions.
+- [x] `scripts/js-tests/form_stepper.test.js` — extend fake-DOM `matches()` with `#id` support; add tests: `sectionComplete` (complete / partial / empty / consent-guard / hidden-conditional), `seedDoneStates` (resume seeds complete-only; form + form-errors seed nothing), `rederiveDone` (empty leave stays white / fill-leave green / empty-after-green returns white / review consent guard).
+
+**Acceptance Criteria:**
+- Given a draft with steps 1–2 complete, when the resume page loads in a real browser, then segments 1–2 are green on arrival and the start step (3) is active.
+- Given the resume above, when the user Backs from empty step 3 into step 2, then step 3 stays white and step 1 stays green.
+- Given any step, when its last unfilled required field is filled and the user leaves, then its segment turns green; when a field is emptied and the user leaves, it returns to white.
+- Given `make test`, `make test-integration` (own Docker DB container), and the form-bug-hunt E2E suite, when run, then all pass unbroken.
+
+## Design Notes
+
+The old `visited` map had one job beyond green-chrome: on `form-errors`, "unvisited earlier steps must not glow teal while the banner says errors need attention". That guarantee survives as "form-errors seeds an empty done-set" — the design intent was never "visits are what count", it was "don't glow prematurely on the error page".
+
+Timer/DOM seam lesson from F3 (field notes): node tests are blind to browser-runtime semantics — the acceptance replay must run in a real browser (agent-browser, Chromium, 375×812), not just suite-green.
+
+## Verification
+
+**Commands:**
+- `node --test scripts/js-tests/*.test.js` — all js-tests green (new stepper tests included)
+- `make test` — unit suites green
+- `cd server && TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://test:test@localhost:54327/righttenantry_test gleam test -- --tag integration` — integration green against own container (`TEST_DB_PORT=54327 bash scripts/reset-test-db.sh` first; port 54321 is contended across worktrees)
+- `bash run_squirrel.sh` — no-op sanity (no SQL touched; skip if clean)
+
+**Manual checks (if no CLI):**
+- Real-browser replay (agent-browser, mobile viewport): local server against own Docker DB + seeded vacancy → fill steps 1–2 → wait for debounced saves → read `continue_token` from `application_draft` → navigate `/apply/:code/resume/<token>?rt_consent_test=1` → assert segment classes per the I/O matrix rows 1–3, with screenshots.
